# Exact cached post-live --all findings; answers explain only the anchors of their class.

[thin] These are the complete source grip's two 1.68 mm thick horizontal wings, 2.40 mm reach and 5.00 mm span, on the full 79.70 mm body span. Both wings and the back begin on the bed. Preserve the complete strip and end wings to read its actual bow-and-engage action; accepted grip/receiver evidence covers removal and fit, not this reference's handling life.
alternatives: A 3.00 mm wing or thicker full strip changes its flexural stiffness and needs taller receiving slots; it ceases to retain the complete source geometry. Shortening the strip or wings changes the spring span/capture area. A rigid multi-piece strip removes the elastic bowing mechanism and adds assembly tolerances.
